p to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 3.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 13.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 7.4 to 25.6. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 2% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 40 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,750 euros, was awarded in June 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove any contract was improperly awarded. Prices near the limit could reflect market rates or budget constraints. Legitimate reasons might explain why contracts are just under the threshold.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review contract [1] to see what was purchased and if it aligns with the body's goals. Look at other contracts to confirm if the same supplier was used for similar services.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["LJL3sXE%2Bse87%2B9FIQYNjeQ%3D%3D","yBco5kcyWiseC9GJQOEBkQ%3D%3D","IGRkA%2FlMZV%2FLIx6q1oPaMg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}